### Phase 2 evidence

- Added `src/dwarfspec/subject_sources.lua`. It defines only `NATIVE` and
  `OVERLAY` through `dwarfspec.immutable_enum.define`; the runtime `ds` table
  exports the exact enum as `ds.ESubjectSource`, and `src/ds.d.lua` declares
  the matching immutable public namespace.
- Added `src/dwarfspec/subject_requests.lua` with documented root, get, and
  tree-capture request records. Omitted source selection defaults to
  `ESubjectSource.NATIVE`; values are accepted only when present in the enum.
  `OVERLAY` requires and preserves one exact nonempty registry name, while
  `NATIVE` rejects any overlay option and every request rejects unknown
  options.
- Added `src/dwarfspec/subject_paths.lua`. Native strings represent one
  unambiguous name and reject `/` with an error directing callers to
  segment-array syntax. Native arrays are copied, must be dense, and retain
  every nonempty string or zero-based nonnegative integral child index without
  splitting slash-bearing names.
- Overlay requests use the Lua-view component path contract because registered
  overlays are adapted Lua views. Existing component resolution now delegates
  to the same component normalizer, preserving its prior slash-delimited,
  reserved-segment, and boundary validation messages.
- Updated the adapter-backed subject descriptor path type to allow native
