### Phase 3 evidence

- Added `src/dwarfspec/native_attachment.lua`. It acquires the current and
  native DF viewscreens through injected getters, requires exact identity,
  rejects a focused DFHack Lua screen explicitly, reads and validates the
  exact `viewscreen.widgets` container, and does all of that before returning
  resources from which a mount record can be created.
- Added the no-argument `ds.mount()` overload using Lua argument count, so
  `ds.mount()` attaches natively while an explicit `ds.mount(nil)` still enters
  and fails the existing component boundary. The overload is declared in
  `src/ds.d.lua`, and `Subject:raw()` now declares its Lua-table or typed-native
  result accurately.
- Added a borrowed interaction target to
  `src/dwarfspec/interaction_target.lua`. It pins the exact native viewscreen,
  re-queries current-screen identity before input or invalidation, rejects a
  transition before dispatch, calls only the injected global invalidator, and
  releases references without screen mutation.
- Added `src/dwarfspec/native_root_adapter.lua` as a deliberately root-only
  adapter. It returns the exact pinned widget container and validates the
  pinned screen before every root operation. Named and indexed traversal
  remains Phase 4 work rather than exposing partial lookup behavior.
- Added `mount_context:mount_native()`. Its mount record keeps
  `host_screen=nil`, pins the borrowed screen separately, never inserts that
  screen into `owned_screens`, installs only DwarfSpec reference cleanup, and
  returns a normal fluent root subject. `ds.viewport()` rejects this record
  before any resize normalization or adapter call.
- Attachment validation occurs before `next_mount_id` advances or run-scoped
  cleanup is registered. Failures after resource creation release the
  interaction target, subject adapter, subject descriptors, mount record, and
  cleanup entries. Tests prove both pre-record acquisition failure and
  post-record validation failure leave no current mount or pending cleanup.
- Added `tests/unit/native_attachment_spec.lua` and extended the interaction
  target, mount-context, and public-command suites. Injected tests cover:
  exact screen/root identity; missing current/native screens; current/native
  mismatch; missing root; source-construction failure; immediate transition
  staleness; normal input through the pinned screen; explicit-`nil`
  preservation; zero host construction/activation; zero owned screens; zero
  show, resize, dismiss, replace, or navigation calls; viewport rejection; and
  normal unmount cleanup.
