### Phase 4 evidence

- Replaced the temporary root-only adapter with
  `src/dwarfspec/native_widget_adapter.lua`. The adapter pins the exact native
  widget root, accepts injected `getWidget` and `getWidgetChildren` services,
  calls `getWidget` once for each normalized path segment, and copies the
  ordered child sequence returned by DFHack without filtering on widget state.
- The production native source in `src/dwarfspec/ds.lua` delegates directly to
  `dfhack.gui.getWidget(parent, segment)` and
  `dfhack.gui.getWidgetChildren(parent)`. Native strings and authoritative
  segment arrays flow through the Phase 2 request/path contracts before
  adapter resolution; component paths retain their existing behavior.
- `mount_context.refresh_views()` now distinguishes the immutable native source
  from Lua component sources. Native names may be absent, duplicated, reserved
  component words, or contain `/`; they are never subjected to component
  `view_id` validation, and every ordered descendant remains discoverable.
- Native subjects retain a copied segment locator, the selected source and
  adapter, and the identity captured at creation. Every `Subject:raw()` or
  fluent operation resolves the locator again, captures the current identity,
  and compares it with the retained identity before returning the exact
  reacquired raw widget.
- Stable identity is injectable for wrapper-based unit fixtures and defaults
  to DFHack typed-reference equality in production. The adapter keeps reached
  identities in a strong linear set so distinct Lua userdata wrappers that
  compare as the same typed DF reference remain recognized without relying on
  Lua table-key identity.
- Native screen currentness is checked before every root, lookup, child,
  identity, name, type, containment, and inspection access. It is checked both
  before and after injected widget helper calls, so a helper cannot cause a
  transition and leave later widget dereferences unguarded.
- Missing lookup diagnostics include the complete type-preserving normalized
  path, failing segment and index, resolved parent name and native type, and
  separate named and zero-based indexed child summaries. Labels are bounded to
  80 characters and each summary is capped at 12 entries with an explicit
  remaining count.
- Removal now reports that the retained widget no longer resolves.
  Same-path replacement reports an identity change and explicitly requires a
  new `ds.get(path)` to select the replacement. Neither condition silently
  rebinds the retained subject.
- Updated `src/ds.d.lua` so `DS.get()` declares string or native segment-array
  paths plus source options. Component regression behavior and exact Lua-table
  subjects remain unchanged.
- Added `tests/unit/native_widget_adapter_spec.lua` and extended the public
  mount suite. Coverage includes named, indexed, mixed, and slash-bearing
  paths; ordered helper calls; stable wrapper identity; exact raw
  reacquisition; invisible/inactive targets; missing segments; deterministic
  bounded diagnostics; removal; replacement; explicit reselection; and screen
  transitions before native service access.
