### Phase 7 evidence

- `src/dwarfspec/ds.lua` now accepts
  `ds.move_pointer(x, y)`, validates nonnegative integral coordinates against
  the current positive integral window dimensions, validates the pinned
  interaction target before and after the window query, and declares the
  overload in `src/ds.d.lua`.
- Subject-derived pointer placement reads current adapter bounds, uses an
  adapter-specific interaction rectangle when available, clips the normalized
  inclusive rectangle to the current window, and reports bounded source, path,
  native type, and normalized bounds when no usable interaction area remains.
- Top-level keyboard and mouse commands, native subjects, and explicit overlay
  subjects all retain one route through `mount.interaction_target` and
  `gui.simulateInput()` with the pinned native viewscreen. Production code does
  not invoke a native callback or overlay `onInput()` directly.
- The DFHack 53.15-r1 source contract was inspected:
  `library/lua/gui.lua` delegates `simulateInput()` to
  `dscreen._doSimulateInput()`;
  `library/LuaApi.cpp` sends those keys through `screen->feed()`; and
  `plugins/overlay.cpp` interposes that feed, dispatches registered overlays,
  and calls the backing native feed only when overlay input is unhandled.
- Existing `EMouseButton` and `EInputState` values are unchanged. Physical
  buttons still default to `CLICK`; explicit down/up and wheel paths retain
  their current virtual pointer, temporary GPS pointer, focus/tracking, and
  run-scoped button-state restoration through the existing pointer adapter.
